"""Source of truth for the 1B folk-triage cases, built from two public vignette sets. Edit here, then run
build_dataset.py.

Sources (raw files and licences in sources/):
  L = Levine et al., Lancet Digit Health 2024 (lay-language rewrites of the Semigran et al. BMJ 2015
      vignettes); github.com/beamlab-hsph/gpt3-clinical-vignettes, MIT. Labels: Emergent / 1 day / 1 week /
      Self-care.
  R = Ramaswamy et al., Nature Medicine 2026, symptoms-only (F) version; github.com/ashwinra-code/gpt-health-eval,
      data CC0. Physician-adjudicated labels: A home / B weeks / C 24-48 h / D emergency department now;
      C/D = edge case where both are acceptable.

Gold mapping: Emergent, D -> emergency; C/D -> urgent; 1 day, 1 week, B, C -> soon; Self-care, A -> self_care.

Each case: id, src_id, gold, clin (Vietnamese translation of the source facts), folk (same facts in folk
wording plus a folk label), folk_terms, remedy (folk remedy the asker plans; every case),
remedy_source / remedy_status (co_nguon_mot_phan = a Vietnamese health page documents the main remedy
ingredients as a folk practice, not that it works; chua_xac_minh = no source found), adapt (every change
beyond translation). Rule: `folk` changes wording and adds a folk label; it never drops, softens or adds a fact.

Texts and remedies were drafted by Claude, then reviewed and edited by the author (2026-11-08; reviewed
sheet in review/cases_reviewed_2026-11-08.csv).
"""

